{"name":"Beeswing","hex":"#f5d297","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beeswing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A filmy, translucent crust found in port and other old wines which have been bottled-aged for a long time.","Cream of tartar; potassium bitartrate; the residual salt of tartaric acid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beeswing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Potassium bitartrate","blocks":[{"text":"Potassium bitartrate, also known as potassium hydrogen tartrate, with formula KC4H5O6, is the potassium acid salt of tartaric acid (a carboxylic acid)—specifically, l-( + )-tartaric acid. Especially in cooking, it is also known as cream of tartar. Tartaric acid and potassium naturally occur in grapes; its crude precipitate form, tartar or wine stone, is a byproduct of winemaking found deposited on top of must barrels, which can be purified."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Potassium-bitartrate-2D-skeletal.svg/330px-Potassium-bitartrate-2D-skeletal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potassium_bitartrate","wikidata":"Q18745"},{"title":"Beeswing (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Beeswing (1833–1854) was a 19th-century British Thoroughbred racehorse from the north of England. In her day, Beeswing was hailed as the greatest mare in Britain and one of the greatest of all time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Beeswing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beeswing_(horse)","wikidata":"Q4880155"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Potassium-3D.png/500px-Potassium-3D.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Potassium-3D.png/500px-Potassium-3D.png?utm_source=en.wikiped